  "id": "BIT-postgresql-2026-116321",
  "summary": "PostgreSQL unterminated name value discloses server memory",
  "details": "Improper null termination in PostgreSQL array element assignment allows a database user to disclose server memory, via changing the final byte of a fixed-length name value to a nonzero byte and passing it to code that treats the value as a C string.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.7, 17.12, 16.16, 15.20, and 14.25 are affected.",
